  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+144y=0,\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=1,\\,{y}^{\u2032}(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=24.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the roots of the characteristic polynomial:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-144 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 12\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =P\\operatorname{cos}\u206112x+Q\\operatorname{sin}\u206112x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-Q=1\\,\u27f9\\,Q=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{\u2032}(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=24,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=-12P\\operatorname{sin}\u206112x+12Q\\operatorname{cos}\u206112x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{\u2032}(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=24$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12P=24\\,\u27f9\\,P=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{cos}\u206112x-\\operatorname{sin}\u206112x.\n$$",
